:[],"description_full":"DiaMedica Therapeutics Inc., a clinical stage biopharmaceutical company, focuses on improving the lives of people suffering from severe ischemic diseases. Its lead candidate is DM199, a pharmaceutically active recombinant form of the human tissue kallikrein-1 protein, which is in Phase 2/3 trials for the treatment of acute ischemic stroke, as well as in Phase 2 to treat preeclampsia, cardio renal disease, and fetal growth restriction. The company develops DM300, which is a recombinant human ulinastatin in the preclinical stage for the treatment of inflammatory diseases, such as acute pancreatitis. The company was formerly known as DiaMedica Inc. and changed its name to DiaMedica Therapeutics Inc. in December 2016. DiaMedica Therapeutics Inc. was incorporated in 2000 and is headquartered in Minneapolis, Minnesota.","ceo_bio":"Mr. Dietrich John Pauls MBA | President, CEO & Director | Age 54 | Compensation: $1.1M (FY2025)","culture_narrative":"Employs approximately 35 people. Stock-based compensation of $110K per employee reflects an ownership culture. Governance score flags elevated compensation governance risk (7/10).","financial_summary":["DiaMedica Therapeutics Inc. is a small-cap healthcare business with a $505M market cap.","Returns on capital run at -40% against a 10% cost of capital, which means the business is destroying value with every dollar it reinvests.","The company is burning through $29M of cash, and without positive owner earnings any valuation rests on hope rather than evidence.","Net dilution runs at 8.6% annually, transferring value from owners to stock-based comp, and insiders hold 28% of the shares, so management thinks like owners because it is one \u2014 the strongest alignment there is."],"sector_headwinds":[{"text":"Piotroski score 2/9 \u2014 the fundamentals are deteriorating on multiple fronts","sev":"red","cat":"quality"},{"text":"Elevated short interest (14.5% of float) \u2014 sophisticated money is betting the oth